Virtio DMA helper — kernel-context provider for `vnet_va_to_pa`
================================================================

Second file of `module oskit.drivers.virtio`. Supplies the one
context-dependent primitive the virtio-net driver needs when it
runs linked directly into the kernel image: converting a CPU-side
VA to a device-side PA.

On every target the kernel currently supports (aarch64 QEMU virt,
x86_64 QEMU `-machine q35`), the 1GB RAM block is identity-mapped
in the kernel's page table — so a kernel VA to RAM *is* the
matching PA. This makes the provider trivial.

When the nic driver is promoted to a standalone boot-module
server, a sibling `virtio_dma_server.lsysl` will provide the same
function using `svc_vm_v2p`. Exactly one of these two files is
linked into any given build.

    module oskit.drivers.virtio

    vnet_va_to_pa(va: i64) -> i64
        va
